{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 EXIT — proven root cause (claimed; attestation certified)\n\n**The root cause is not the misnamed variable. It is that the DOCUMENTED credential-delivery\nmechanism structurally cannot reach a GUI-launched process, and nothing detects that.**\n\n### Evidence\n\n1. `docs/mcp-client-setup.md:26` and `examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:9` both prescribe\n   `export MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX=\"…\"` — a **shell export**.\n2. On this host the variable is absent from the **launchd** environment, which is what a\n   GUI-launched macOS app inherits — under BOTH names:\n       launchctl getenv MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX  -> unset\n       launchctl getenv REBAR_CODEX_PAT       -> unset\n3. It is absent from every shell rc file too (`~/.zshrc`, `~/.zprofile`, `~/.bash_profile`,\n   `~/.profile`) — so it was never persistently exported at all, only ever transiently in one\n   shell.\n4. No document in the repo mentions `launchctl`, GUI launches, login shells, or environment\n   inheritance. Grep across `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, `docs/mcp-auth.md` and\n   `examples/mcp-clients/` returns nothing.\n\n### Why the 2026-08-25 smoke passed — the verification path is not the usage path\n\n`creased-childlike-jackal` verified the three clients by invoking them from a **shell**\n(`claude -p \"call rebar list_tickets\"`, `codex mcp list`). A shell-launched process DOES inherit\na transient export made in that same shell, so the smoke exercised the one path that works and\nnever touched the desktop path. The green smoke was therefore never evidence about GUI launches.\n\n**This corrects the ticket's premise.** The description reasons that a passing 2026-08-25 smoke\nmakes the current state 'post-verification drift/regression rather than an unimplemented\nendpoint'. On this evidence the GUI path was never verified and plausibly never worked; this is\ncloser to an unimplemented delivery path than to a regression. I am not asserting it never worked\n— I cannot see the host's state on 08-25 — but the smoke does not support the regression claim.\n\n### The name drift is real but NOT load-bearing\n\n`~/.codex/config.toml` does say `bearer_token_env_var = \"REBAR_CODEX_PAT\"` against a canonical\n`MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`. Correcting it alone would change NOTHING: neither name is set anywhere\nthe GUI process can see. Any fix that only reconciles the name would leave the bug live while\nappearing to address it.\n\n### Consequence for AC2, which is already satisfied\n\nThe repo is already single-sourced on `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX` (`docs/mcp-auth.md:286,294,322`,\n`docs/mcp-client-setup.md:26,74`, `examples/mcp-clients/README.md:11,21`,\n`examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:19`) and it is ALREADY PINNED by\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py:58`. `REBAR_CODEX_PAT` appears nowhere in\nthe repository. So AC2's 'single-source the canonical name' work does not exist; what is missing\nis detection of a hand-edited LOCAL config that no committed test can observe.\n\n### Legitimacy\n\nThis is a genuine defect, not working-as-designed: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` presents Codex as a\nsupported client and gives a setup that cannot work for the desktop application, without\nqualifying that it is CLI-only.\n\nNo credential value was read, printed, or transmitted at any point in this investigation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787856740704723001,"uuid":"0a4d8d4a-cd94-4f70-926c-8563749bd0cf"}